## Nothing on screen?

Work through these in order:

**Wrong baud rate.** The most common cause. Symptom: garbled characters instead of readable text means the speed is wrong but the cable is fine. A completely blank screen usually means something else.

**Wrong cable type.** <!-- TO FILL: what you actually used, and what didn't work -->

**Adapter not recognised.** Check Device Manager (Windows) or `dmesg | tail` (Linux) after plugging it in.

**Connected too late.** Some appliances only emit output during a short window at power-on. Have the terminal open *before* switching the unit on.

